course: dictionary
lesson: 10373
title: Treasure: one word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word treasure can mean different things. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. In «Gold does not rust or tarnish and is soft enough to shape, so it has been treasured for thousands of years», the clues are gold, rust and shape, so treasured means kept carefully because it is valued.
explain: Look at the word's job in the sentence. If treasure is a thing, it is a noun. If it is an action, like treasured or treasuring, it is a verb. Ask yourself: is someone doing something to the word, or is it a thing? That tells you which kind of word it is.
explain: Sometimes treasure is a person. Informal means relaxed everyday speech. If someone says, «She is a treasure!» about a helpful neighbour, they mean she is very kind or helpful. Always check the clues before you pick a meaning.
fact: Treasure can be a noun (a treasure, treasures) or a verb (treasure, treasured, treasuring).
fact: «Treasure» can mean gold, silver, jewels or other valuable things, often hidden.
fact: «A treasure» can mean anything that is very precious to you.
fact: «To treasure» something means to keep it carefully and love it because it means a lot to you.
fact: Informal: «a treasure» can mean a person who is very kind or helpful.
exercise: «Pirates buried the treasure on a sandy island.» What does treasure mean here? | A map drawn with a red X | A kind sailor | A big wooden ship | *Gold, silver and jewels, often hidden
exercise: Mum says, «My old school photos are my treasure.» What does treasure mean here? | Something hidden under the floor | Money she has to pay back | *Something very precious to her | A place where rain falls
exercise: «Your phone is a little treasure chest worth recycling.» What does treasure chest suggest? | *A place where valuable metals are kept, so the phone is worth saving | A box full of old toys | A pirate ship at sea | A chest that is empty and useless
test: Which sentence uses treasure as a verb? | *«I treasure every card my grandad gave me.» | «The treasure chest was empty.» | «Pirates buried the treasure.» | «The treasure map has an X on it.»
test: «When you collect nature treasures for school, take only a few.» What does treasures mean in this sentence? | Rocks used for building | Money from a shop | *Natural things, like shells or leaves, that you find | Pirate gold buried in the sand
exam: In «Gold ... has been treasured for thousands of years», what does treasured mean? | Dug up from the ground | Sold cheaply at a market | Melted down into coins | *Kept carefully and loved because it is valued
